# 3. The historical analogy is interesting

If we're comparing the languages you asked about previously:

```text
BASIC
   ↓
Visual Basic
   ↓
Windows GUI + event-driven programming
```

```text
Pascal
   ↓
Object Pascal
   ↓
Delphi
   ↓
Windows GUI + RAD
```

C++ took a somewhat different route:

```text
C
 ↓
C++
 ↓
 ┌───────────────┬───────────────┐
 ↓               ↓               ↓
Win32           MFC             Qt
 ↓               ↓               ↓
Windows GUI     Windows GUI     Cross-platform GUI
```

So if you wanted a rough historical analogy:

| Language             | Famous GUI development environment/framework |
| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| BASIC                | **Visual Basic**                             |
| Pascal/Object Pascal | **Delphi**                                   |
| C++                  | **MFC / Qt / Win32**                         |
| C#                   | **WinForms / WPF / .NET MAUI**               |
| Java                 | **AWT / Swing / JavaFX**                     |

